  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "src/ui/AppShell.test.tsx",
      "content": "Resolve the stale status inside an awaited `act` boundary instead of waiting 20 ms. The timer does not explicitly flush React's pending work; if the stale-update guard regresses, the resulting update is also scheduled outside `act`, which can produce warnings and make the negative assertions timing-dependent. For example, use `await act(async () =\u003e { resolveStale(takenOver() as never); });` before checking the active facade's UI.",
      "existing_code": "    resolveStale(takenOver() as never);\n    await new Promise((resolve) =\u003e setTimeout(resolve, 20));",
      "start_line": 1332,
      "end_line": 1333,
      "category": "test",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/ReviewCard.tsx",
      "content": "The badges are hidden after a closing sale, but the header still has `aria-describedby={reasonIds...}` and the visually hidden reason spans are still rendered below it. Screen-reader users therefore continue to hear the old open-position warnings when focusing the header beside the closing receipt. Apply the `soldOut` guard to the description IDs and reason spans as well, and cover the header's accessible description in the closing-sale test.",
      "existing_code": "            {!soldOut \u0026\u0026 labels.map(({ label }) =\u003e (",
      "start_line": 142,
      "end_line": 142,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/ExitReceipt.tsx",
      "content": "Handle the `Due` classification separately rather than treating every value other than `DueInReviewAfterNext` as next Review. A backdated sale (for example, a Monday sale recorded on Tuesday) can have its debt anchor at or before the previous close, so `classifyDue` returns `Due` and the Review asks for it now. Both receipt messages nevertheless say next Review. Use an explicit classification-to-message mapping and add a backdated-sale case to verify the receipt agrees with the Review.",
      "existing_code": "        {closeReview?.kind === 'Debt' \u0026\u0026 closed \u0026\u0026 \u003cp\u003e{`Recorded. ${trade.plan.underlying} is closed. Its Close Review is due in ${later(dueIn?.closeReview) ? 'the Review after next' : 'the next Review'}.`}\u003c/p\u003e}\n        {postCommit.reflection.kind === 'Debt' \u0026\u0026 postCommit.reflection.debt.requires?.includes('PlanDepartureReason') \u0026\u0026 \u003cp\u003e{`${closeReview?.kind === 'Debt' \u0026\u0026 closed ? '' : 'Recorded. '}Why you left the Plan is owed at ${later(dueIn?.reflection) ? 'the Review after next' : 'the next Review'}.`}\u003c/p\u003e}",
      "start_line": 167,
      "end_line": 168,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/ReviewCard.tsx",
      "content": "The sold-out guard removes the status and P\u0026L, but the preceding `trade.summary` still renders the old open position (for example, “Long 100 shares @ $50.10”) beside the closing receipt. That summary is derived from the held quantity, so the card still presents the Trade as held after selling everything. Hide or replace that summary when `soldOut` is true, and include a populated summary in the regression test.",
      "existing_code": "            {!soldOut \u0026\u0026 \u003cspan className=\"review-card-remains\"\u003e{remainsText(trade.progress, line?.action, line?.closeReview ?? false, line?.needs ?? [])}\u003c/span\u003e}{' '}",
      "start_line": 141,
      "end_line": 141,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/ReviewView.tsx",
      "content": "Entries are only added to `soldOut`; no successful reread clears them. A Trade closed after the session cutoff can remain in the walked Review (the card explicitly supports this lifecycle). After dismissing its receipt and successfully refreshing, its freshly read Now box, P\u0026L, labels and Action status therefore remain hidden for the rest of this mounted view. Clear the relevant sold-out state when the refreshed card is applied, while retaining it if the refresh fails.",
      "existing_code": "  const [soldOut, setSoldOut] = useState\u003cReadonlySet\u003cstring\u003e\u003e(() =\u003e new Set());\n  const closedSale = (tradeId: string) =\u003e setSoldOut((current) =\u003e new Set(current).add(tradeId));",
      "start_line": 465,
      "end_line": 466,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/coordinators/trade-workflows/record-position-change.ts",
      "content": "This adds a fallible Market Data read after persistence.commit has already succeeded. If that read rejects (for example, an IndexedDB read fails), the mutation guard reports StorageFailure/RuntimeNotWritable instead of returning Recorded, even though the sale and debts are durable. The user sees a failed save and no receipt for a sale that actually closed the trade. Resolve the optional due classification before committing, or isolate failures of this post-commit enrichment so they cannot replace a successful mutation result. Add a test where this query rejects after the commit.",
      "existing_code": "    postCommit: { trade, derivation, reflection: outcome, ...(close \u0026\u0026 { closeReview: close.outcome }), ...(await dueInOf(deps, trade.plan.underlying, outcome, close?.outcome)) },",
      "start_line": 534,
      "end_line": 534,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    }
